  "name": "luh-ct-data-inner-lattice-channels",
  "notes": "This dataset contains micro-computed tomography images of an additively manufactured (powder bed fusion of metals using a laser beam, PBF-LB/M) demonstrator part intended for thermal applications. The part consists of branching internal fluid channels and has been generated via _Algorithms-Aided Design_ using the software _Grasshopper_.\r\n\r\n* __Outer Dimensions:__ 30 x 29 x 56 mm³\r\n* __Wall Thickness:__ 0.6 mm\r\n* __Channel Diameters:__\r\n\t* 4 mm (Inner Channels)\r\n\t* 8 mm (Inlet + Outlet)\r\n* __Material:__ 1.2709 (MS1)\r\n* __PBF-LB Machine:__ EOS EOSINT M 280\r\n* __µCT Scanner:__ Bruker SkyScan 1275\r\n\r\n![Volumetric Representation](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/360098ca-9e6f-47ef-8ca5-aec6acb8a278/resource/019ca72d-c462-4497-bd9b-1bc3ff388858/download/ct_50_um_rec0000_voi_a.png\r\n)\r\nVolumetric representation of the obtained CT data\r\n\r\n### References:\r\n\r\nThis data was obtained in the context of the bachelor thesis:\r\n\r\n* Messmann, C. O.: _Generation of Biomimetic Structures to Increase the Thermal Performance of Additively Manufactured Heat Exchangers_, 2022, Leibniz University Hannover\r\n\r\n### Acknowledgements:\r\n\r\n* The project _“Computer tomograph for optomechatronic systems”_ was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) - Project number 432176896.",
